NAME
    framelog - sample a memory value once per frame

SYNOPSIS
    framelog add <space> <addr> [<width>]
    framelog list
    framelog show <id> [<count>]
    framelog clear <id>
    framelog remove <id>

DESCRIPTION
    Unlike 'watch' (triggered by an actual read/write), a frame log samples
    its value once every frame regardless of whether anything touched it -
    useful for 'what does this value do over time' questions a write watch
    can't answer, e.g. a counter written once at level start but read every
    frame afterward. <width> is 1, 2, or 4 bytes (default 1).

EXAMPLES
    framelog add WRAM 1fb0 2
    framelog show 1
